### Auto-merge policy

`.github/workflows/auto-merge.yml` squash-merges **every** pull request whose `__HARNESS_CI_WORKFLOW__` run (and review, if any) is green, pinned to the validated SHA, then deletes its branch; docs-only pull requests (every file in `docs/**`, `**.md`, `LICENSE`, `.gitignore`) merge at once, without CI. **Never merged unattended**: a pull request touching Claude instruction files (`CLAUDE_GATE_RE`: `.claude/`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.githooks/`, `.mcp.json`, this workflow, the gate and what it runs or reads; the project's own in `PROJECT_GATE_RE`) or from a `claude/issue-*` head, the Dependabot bumps the gate holds (majors, Action minors), and a pull request that deletes or rewrites lines of an existing test (`TEST_HOLD_RE`, empty until the project fills it) — marked ready, merged by hand. Draft does **not** pause a pull request: cancel its CI run or close it. A merge here emits no `push` event. A workflow-touching pull request may be refused at merge while CI is green: merge it by hand, never grant `workflows: write`. A pull request runs its own copy of the workflows: the ruleset on the default branch (code-owner review for `.github/workflows/**`) is what holds one that rewrites them. → `docs/conventions/auto-merge-policy.md`
